y.org/articles/foreign-influence-in-the-campaign-against-american-ai", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "THE MONEY BEHIND EVERYTHING AGAINST TRUMP AND AMERICA COMES OUT OF CHINA...CHINA IS ASSHOE!", "last_comment_created": 1788202651318, "content": "", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 3, "score_up": 49, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"description": "A new Bitcoin Policy Institute research paper documents a multi-year foreign influence campaign aimed at slowing the United States' artificial intelligence buildout. The report traces three convergent vectors: Chinese state media outlets CGTN, China Daily, and Global Times, alongside Russia's RT, running attributed campaigns against US AI data centers and export controls; a CCP-aligned US 501(c)(3) network funded by Shanghai-based expatriate Neville Roy Singham, which has produced parallel domestic content opposing American AI infrastructure for nearly five years; and more than $2 billion routed through foreign-tied charitable vehicles \u2014 including Swiss billionaire Hansj\u00f6rg Wyss and the Oak Foundation \u2014 into US advocacy groups driving the anti-data-center push. BPI maps how these streams converged on the Sanders\u2013Ocasio-Cortez AI Data Center Moratorium Act and 54 local moratoriums, and offers policy recommendations on FARA enforcement, foreign-funding disclosure, and transparency in state and local AI infrast", "large_image": "Ewl68TiXkWSJsNns.png", "title": "Foreign Influence in the Campaign against American AI | Bitcoin Policy Institute"}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "link", "uuid": "1ATV3Wj3RZ", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin":